# Secrets for the ChatNyto broker deployment.
#
# Copy to deploy/.env.prod (gitignored) and fill in. Values may reference a
# password manager — deploy-remote.sh resolves them on YOUR machine and
# streams the result to the server's tmpfs, so nothing secret is written to
# the server's disk or committed here.
#
#   cp deploy/.env.prod.example deploy/.env.prod

# Accounts allowed on the broker, space separated user:password pairs.
# Give each person or device its own; they are what you type into the app's
# "Add network" dialog.
MQTT_USERS="nyto:$(pass show chatnyto.prod/MQTT_NYTO) phone:$(pass show chatnyto.prod/MQTT_PHONE)"

# Account the health check uses; it must also appear in MQTT_USERS.
MQTT_HEALTH_USER=nyto
MQTT_HEALTH_PASSWORD=$(pass show chatnyto.prod/MQTT_NYTO)

# Cloudflare Tunnel token. Create the tunnel in the Zero Trust dashboard and
# add a public hostname route:
#   <your domain>  path /mqtt  ->  http://mqtt:9001
# Nothing else exposes the broker.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=$(pass show chatnyto.prod/CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN)

# The address people type into the app. Everything else about the connection
# is published at https://$PUBLIC_HOST/.well-known/chatnyto.json, so this is
# the only thing they ever have to know.
PUBLIC_HOST=supa-tech.com
PUBLIC_NAME="Supa Tech"

# The account the app picks up from that file. Give it its own entry in
# MQTT_USERS: it is handed to every device that joins, so it should not be
# an account you also use yourself.
APP_USER=app
APP_PASSWORD=$(pass show chatnyto.prod/MQTT_APP)

# --- voice calls over mobile data (optional) ---------------------------------
# Two people on the same WiFi call each other directly and need nothing here.
# Two people on mobile data have no address the other can reach, and the call
# needs a meeting point: that is what these are.
#
# Setting them switches on a coturn container. It is the one part of the stack
# that cannot go through the Cloudflare tunnel — TURN is UDP — so open these
# ports on the server first:
#
#   3478/udp  3478/tcp  49160-49200/udp
#
# Leave them unset and calls still work on a shared network, and the app falls
# back to relaying the audio over MQTT everywhere else.
#TURN_USER=chatnyto
#TURN_PASSWORD=$(pass show chatnyto.prod/TURN)
#TURN_PUBLIC_IP=203.0.113.10
